  "_comment": "ADR-0562 §10.26 twenty-second strangler move, SUB-BATCH (b): home the intelligence capability's MANIFEST-CLEAN PURE KERNEL/DOMAIN FLOOR from the oya/intelligence junk-drawer into the ratified bare-root `intelligence/` capability (sub-batch (a) already established intelligence/ from cloud/cloud-intelligence per specs/reachability-registry.json §10.26(a); this is the first of the b-g sub-batches homing the 124 oya/intelligence crates). This batch moves 15 dependency-SINK crates: 8 ADR-0083 kernels (pure-types + sync-traits, EMPTY [dependencies]) + capability-domain + 6 domains (each either EMPTY deps or a single DOWN edge to libs/oya-data-boundary-kernel; ZERO intra-intelligence out-edges). SINK-FIRST so nothing else must reference a not-yet-moved intelligence crate. FACE = core for all 15 (ADR-0570: a cutover-stable kernel-tier port is PERMITTED in core; mirrors existing intelligence/core/{kernel,tool-compat-kernel,translation-kernel,wire-kernel} + messaging/core/domain). The acyclicity gate's owning_service() is STRUCTURALLY BLIND to intelligence/* (unclassified_root), so face direction is hand-verified: every moved crate is a sink (ZERO ../../{adapters,facade} edges possible), core placement non-inverting. De-brand per ADR-0532/0533 + naming grammar: cargo name = intelligence-<leaf> (strip oya-intelligence-, prepend intelligence-), matching every existing intelligence/ destination crate. Pre-existing gate-bound registry/catalog/oya-intelligence-<leaf>.yaml records re-keyed to intelligence-<leaf>.yaml as content-preserving artifact co-moves (catalog is filename-keyed, carries no internal crate-name field), reached by the existing registry/catalog/ prefix. Contract surfaces (a) workspace glob intelligence/*/*, (b) registry absorbs_current_dirs {intelligence, oya/intelligence}, (c) membership scan_roots+allowed_top_level_dirs intelligence, (d) acyclicity crate_root_globs intelligence/*/* + unclassified_roots intelligence are ALL pre-satisfied by sub-batch (a). DEFERRED (not guessed) to a later sub-batch that CO-HOMES their non-crate service-manifest records: the 6 microservice-entangled kernels (model-routing/assist-draft/guardrails/context-aware-retrieval/eval/attribution) referenced by specs/microservices/intelligence.json ($ref+test_ref) + oya/intelligence/manifest.json, plus credential-resolver-domain (2 manifest refs) and evidence-domain (specs/microservices/ontology.json ref) — a crate-first move would strand their GREEN service-manifest refs (the crate-first doctrine's already-orphaned safety does not hold for these), so they wait until the batch that also re-keys those manifest surfaces. Also DEFERRED: the api/usecase/app/worker/adapter/rest/cli crates (facade-vs-adapters face needs per-crate hand-verification) and the misfiled cross-capability crates (oya-collab-*, oya-shuffle-sharding, oya-codeview-cli). Non-crate artifacts (oya/intelligence/slos capability SLOs, manifest.json, docs, contracts) stay for phase-2 (task #62) per crate-first strangler mode. Refs #1325.",
